{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-fix-wire-ado/batch-conflict-delete-readback",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-ADO-1",
    "ADO-BATCH",
    "ADO-VALUES"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-ado-1b/batch-conflict-delete: the final read-back Execute failed with \"Record is deleted\", so the stored rows after the conflict were never seen, and its cause (the reading connection or the data) was not separated. A client static batch-optimistic recordset of SELECT ID, Code, V, V2, S FROM W ORDER BY ID is opened on a read-write copy of r-ado-1b-main; a second Connection runs \"DELETE FROM W WHERE ID = 2\" (Errors cleared); S of rows 1, 2 and 3 is set to \"c1\", \"c2\", \"c3\"; UpdateBatch(adAffectAll) and the Errors; each row's Status, ID, S, OriginalValue and UnderlyingValue; Filter = adFilterConflictingRecords (RecordCount, rows) and Filter none; Resync(adAffectAll, adResyncUnderlyingValues), the rows again, a second UpdateBatch (Errors) and the rows. The stored rows (ID <= 4) are then read three ways, each with its own errors read and cleared: Execute on the first Connection, Execute on a third fresh Connection, and a DAO read-only snapshot. Asks which staged changes reach the file and what each of the three reads returns.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
  "pathBinding": "attempt-local-copy",
